        {
            "id": "0e174a4a-53d7-ef11-8ee9-7c1e5235d924",
            "subject": "ID0400940-DC/Si-D/IL-[MP / P4 170000462] Slow Charging on Type 2 Charging Stations CRM:00641000967",
            "body": "Dear Mr.Orel Lachiani,\nHope you are doing well\nI trust this email finds you in good health. We have received a technical support request from\nZEN-EV\nin your region regarding the following product:\nProduct:\nSicharge D - Charging Center\nMain Asset:\nMP / P4 170000462\nCharger ID/Serial No.:\n3nmTN4\nProblem Description: Slow Charging on Type 2 Charging Stations\nWe have analyzed the few sessions and observed that the Electric Vehicle Supply Equipment (EVSE) is consistently fulfilling the current requested by the Electric Vehicle (EV). The EV’s requested current (EV_TarCur[A]) is being accurately provided by the charger (NowCur[A]).\nTo clarify further, the power delivery of the charger is entirely based on the EV's demand. For instance, if the EV requests a current of 200A and the voltage is 700V, the charger will deliver approximately 140kW of power. Please find below the relevant log excerpts, which illustrate that the EV's request is being met by the EVSE: So in this our first initial analysis we suspect that problem might be with EV so need to check also brand of EVs which has been charged by this charger.\nUpon reviewing our asset database, we found that the product is no longer under warranty since [\n4/8/2024\n], as a result, we are transferring the case to the regional queue.\nKindly communicate with the customer and provide the necessary service support and/or offer. We have already informed the customer that a regional representative will be in touch shortly.\nShould you require further remote or expert support, please order it via PMD.\nFor additional information, please visit the Service Collaboration SharePoint. If you need assistance with ordering Expert Support, feel free to reach out to Sousa, Afonso (SI E CS SD) at\nafonso-sousa@siemens.com\nor Teodoso, Rui (SI E CS SD ES) at\nrui.teodoso@siemens.com\n.\nWith best regards,\neMobility Tech Support Team -\nAbhinav Malokar\nPlease do not change the subject of this Email when replying to it",
